---
date: 2026-03-09T00:00:00-04:00
---

The Prime Meridian Sub Transit Nexus is the building that runs [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/index|Sableclutch]]'s share of the [[Org/Prime Meridian/index|Prime Meridian]] rail system. It stands one story tall with a basement, behind a gate with guarded booths, and like its copies elsewhere along the horizon it is not open to the public.

Its elevators do not climb. Each one slips a single direction, starward or voidward, to the identical building fifty worlds the same way; the Org has taken a skyscraper apart into one-story floors and spread them across the horizon. [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] knew the building on sight. The Party came here looking for [[Org/Prime Meridian/Rapid Connection|Rapid Connection]], and were let in the back to meet one of the Heart's servants before being put out again.

The Party came back with a [[People/Kellum Quinn|Kellum Quinn]] and were let in this time. Beyond the public lobby the building is a warren of catwalk flooring a foot above the ground and walls, floor and ceiling packed with cable coverings, pipes and tubes that hum and pulse with moving fluid, built to be hard for an intruder to read. The workers pass in silence, their heads turning together, each with rods of dull metal set into arm and throat. [[People/Hogan Voss Darkmoor|Archmechanic Darkmoor]] keeps an office on the second floor, plain but for a pen, an inkwell and a small plaque, and from the lobby a freight elevator descends for what feels like five minutes into the fane of [[Org/Prime Meridian/Rapid Connection|Rapid Connection]], a ring of stone over thousands of gears of the same dull metal that runs in the staff. The elevator and the fane had not been used in decades.

On 3 March, as the Party came back up from the fane with keystone 14, [[Org/Concordia/index|Concordia]] came through the front door for it: two agents, [[Org/Concordia/People/Crawford Reeves|Crawford Reeves]] and [[Org/Concordia/People/Louis Maller|Louis Maller]], with six Happy Time Enforcers and an incident already made at the gatehouse outside. The Party, with the Archmechanic driving workers' bodies to fight for them, killed the agents and the enforcers in the lobby.

After the fight [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] studied the blue light that had flashed from the dead enforcers' eyes as they expired. He knew the glow from the constructs that work for [[Org/Belvedere|Belvedere]], which shine the same blue along their skin and veins, and guessed that the Concordia enforcers had some mechanical augmentation, though he had not examined a body and could not be sure. He searched the two ranked agents and found no identification. [[Org/Concordia/People/Crawford Reeves|Crawford Reeves]] carried a small green stone, opaque and faintly translucent, that was magic and did nothing. [[Org/Concordia/People/Louis Maller|Louis Maller]] wore boots with detachable heels on actuators; the heels were clockwork, and when fixed to a shoe they add a spring to the step.

The workers of the Submechanitor hauled the bodies away deeper into the facility. Low-Mechanitor Exitum-ρ-15 walked the Party back to their car at the rear of the lot and saw them out the back exit; they still were not given the run of the building. The Archmechanic asked them to fax the fence at the bar or reach him at the frequency they had used before.
